# Toy clock-race model: A1/A2 sanity check (time in units of Theta = log 1/alpha; delta = 0.05)
# Columns: t/Th = time; tau/Th = int ||r||_n dt (A2 'effective time'); T = #gates; dep = depth;
# kappa = top eigenvalue of the centred Gram matrix of active gates; k*tau^2 = A2.3 size bound;
# A1-kl / A1-bern = Theorem A1 bounds (kl inversion / Bernstein form) on the test 0-1 error.

### par2  n=64  variant=LS  (#depth-1 candidates after merging: n/a)
  t/Th tau/Th   T dep  kappa  k*tau^2  trLoss  trErr  teErr  A1-kl A1-bern
  1.05   1.02   1   1   0.95     1.00  0.0000  0.000  0.000  0.206   0.461

